From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: conhost: a pseudo console waits for its input pipe's client

node-pty -- VS Code's integrated terminal, and other Electron terminals --
creates a pseudo console on the server ends of two named pipes before any
client has connected, and connects them afterwards. conhost's input thread
started reading at once, got STATUS_PIPE_LISTENING, and ended: the shell
came up and printed its prompt, but nothing typed ever reached it. It now
waits for the client and keeps reading.

Gate: test/devtools-gate.sh (conpty).
---
--- a/programs/conhost/conhost.c
+++ b/programs/conhost/conhost.c
@@ -1765,6 +1765,15 @@
             if ((status = NtWaitForSingleObject( event, FALSE, NULL ))) break;
             status = io.Status;
         }
+        /* a pseudo console's input may be the server end of a named pipe that
+         * nobody has connected to yet: node-pty (VS Code's terminal) creates
+         * the pseudo console first and connects afterwards. Wait for the
+         * client rather than giving up on input for good. */
+        if (status == STATUS_PIPE_LISTENING)
+        {
+            Sleep( 20 );
+            continue;
+        }
         if (status) break;
 
         EnterCriticalSection( &console_section );
